HISTORY OF THE RFS AI PACK 2.0:}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The RFS AI Pack 2.0 is something that has lived and died many times as a project dating as far back as the turn of 2004. The 1.5 release of the pack is credited to \'93Radio F Disturbedware\'94, a hybridization of my username and that of TheDisturbedOne whose poking around with UI files allowed AI teams to have six robots instead of the default three. This discovery was used in version 1.2 to expand all of the AI teams. The discovery was truly groundbreaking and gave The RFS AI Pack a lot of attention. The AI pack was so prevalent that copies of RA2 that were distributed on torrent websites came pre-patched with The RFS AI Pack. Regrettably I took most of the spotlight because I was an annoying prick around the turn of the millennium and I feel that in hindsight I never gave TheDisturbedOne the recognition he deserved. I never would've figured out the six robot AI team thing on my own, that was all him.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Back in 2004 I was on track to produce the next installment of The RFS AI Pack, named version 1.7 at the time. However also around this time I became sidetracked with an old love. The \'93Radio F\'94 in \'93Radio F Software\'94 comes from a comedy troupe I was a part of from 1995 to 1999; I was a performer in the group but my contributions largely involved writing and producing the group's printed content. Around 2004 I was revisiting websites like Seanbaby and Something Awful and enjoying their video game content. When I was with Radio F one of the big things we were known for was our lampooning of crappy video games. I became enthralled with doing this again on my own so the budding website I'd built for Radio F Disturbedware was taken down and replaced with a familiar face that veterans of the RA2 community will surely remember: Radio F Software Headquarters, more affectionately known as \'93RFSHQ\'94. May 9, 2004 was a red letter day for me as it was when my first video game article, a snarky \'93review\'94 of the NES game The Adventures of Bayou Billy, went live.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
I immediately became absorbed in working on RFSHQ. I really enjoyed going back to the type of content that made me happy and productive years prior. I was so enamored by it all that The RFS AI Pack 1.7 withered on the vine and when the website was redesigned to diminish RA2's significance on it the AI pack effectively died.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
RFSHQ was a mixed bag for me. I was enjoying my stint as a webmaster and my friend goose (of GameTechMods notoriety) had joined forces with me to bring the website to a bigger audience. He helped me get set up with a proper dot-com and everything (which he still owns to this day, though the destination website is currently offline as of the release of this mod). I was a bit of a loudmouth though and I would wind up writing checks with my mouth that my ass couldn't cash, to use a turn of phrase to summarize my time there. I feel I did a lot of personal groundbreaking with RFSHQ because it allowed me to really spread my wings and expand to more than just writing about video games. Everything wound up on RFSHQ; monster trucks, energy drinks, BattleBots, the list goes on. My current project of eight years, BattleBots Update, was birthed by RFSHQ back in 2008. By 2008 however I'd started making some really dumb ass life decisions and on a whim I departed from RFSHQ leaving it in the hands of goose. Goose would eventually turn RFSHQ into the notably successful social gaming platform TrackMill Games. Buried somewhere in that website is the original vBulletin database that RFSHQ ran on from 2005-2008.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Around 2010 I got a wild hair and decided I wanted to take another swing at the AI pack. Still going by the development version of 1.7 I posted to GameTechMods that I was officially working on the pack. I was inspired after a television deal between BattleBots and CBS Sports Network failed to produce a show. (\'93I needed my fix again.\'94) Development was going well and I was designing entire teams of robots for the pack. The RA1 & RA2 \'93Revenge\'94 teams in this pack contain robots that were literally designed and skinned in 2010 that managed to stay alive through various hard drive and computer upgrades. Other robots that feature in this pack, such as Auto-Axe and Super Thumperizer, made the jump as well and are in their corresponding teams. Things were looking up, though in a matter of a couple of months my enthusiasm for the project petered out and I quietly swept it under the rug. I was in college at the time and although I can't remember what classes I was taking in the first semester of 2010 that was close to my graduation so they were probably senior level courses that demanded more of my attention than I could warrant giving to an RA2 AI pack.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Years would pass and in 2014 I found myself with a cushy IT job and some time to kill while on the clock. I started posting on GameTechMods again and took an interest in the various tournaments happening on the forum. Unlike what I was used to back in the early days of the game \'96 people battling each other online \'96 these new tournaments were organized by one person who you sent all your bots to and they'd write AI for them and have the robots fight each other while being AI controlled. It took some getting used to but it was fun to watch the fights unfold. I started designing robots again and a couple of them, Jeremy Clarkson and The Legend of Bryce Genesis, appear in this pack. At the same time I started over fresh and was working on The RFS AI Pack once more. This time I was working on it without telling anyone because I was embarrassed about what happened in 2010. Among the robots I designed during this era of the pack are the ones in the \'93RFS Greatest Hits\'94 team as well as Hot Pursuit, Creep, Mad Max, and Runaway Rocket. My reasoning for stopping work on this iteration of the pack was simple. I lost that cushy job and had to quickly uproot myself and move across the state to a cheaper place to live. I just didn't work on the AI pack anymore once I made the move.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
I wouldn't touch the AI pack again until 2022 when I realized RA2's 20}{{\*\updnprop10000}\up10\rtlch \ltrch\loch
th}{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
 anniversary was approaching in February of the following year. I decided I was going to make this god damn pack a reality for the game's upcoming milestone. I started work by unraveling all of the previous attempts I'd done, figuring out which backups had which bots, and then carefully organizing them into a proto AI pack where I could test them out. I had about five or six teams' worth of designs that I could salvage from my attempts in 2010 and 2014 as well as designs that I could remember from the 2004 iteration that I'd need to rebuild in the game. That averaged out to about eight teams of which I needed fifteen to complete the pack so that means about half the pack is proper vintage and the latter half are new designs I created in 2022 special for this pack.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
I didn't want to stop at just making robots though, I wanted to include more with this pack because I intended to go out with a bang. I know fuck all about 3D modeling but I did remember that back in the AceUplink days I wrote a tutorial on how to reskin components and save them as new parts to use in the game. It's how I turned the large CO2 tank into a fire extinguisher once upon a time. I had to dig through the Internet Archive's snapshots of AceUplink to find these damned things and amazingly there were snapshots of the forum thread I posted way back in 2003 explaining the process. A lot of other threads were saved containing a whole bunch of embarrassing posts from me too so digging through the muck was a real banger of an experience that I'm not eager to do again anytime soon. It's been 20 years. I'd forgotten how to reskin components and write AI so I had to rely on crappy tutorials I wrote when I was still in high school to relearn the process. The fact that you are reading this right now means my ancient ass was able to figure it out and make it happen. It wasn't easy, and I had to learn how to use Paint.net to make TGA image files.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
It took 19 years but The RFS AI Pack 2.0 has finally been released, a stock AI pack featuring 90 new robots designed over the many years of this mod's turbulent history. Unlike the previous versions' robots I actually made some custom skins for many of these bots as opposed to doing their paint jobs entirely in RA2. Can I just add how much of a pain in the ass this was? I'm impressed RA2 still runs on Windows 10 seeing as how it came out in the era of Windows XP but god damn I was only ever able to export one custom paint job at a time before the game would crash on me. I also couldn't set the wiring for more than one robot without the game fucking up. Basically what I am trying to tell you is putting this pack together took a literal act of god and I'm glad the development process is over. But more importantly I am glad this pack is done. I've been through some shit in the past 20 years to put it lightly and I know that by completing this AI pack I've restored some kind of balance in the universe. Somewhere, young RFS is happy that his dreams of a big follow-up to The RFS AI Pack have finally been realized.}
\par \pard\plain \s0{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af5\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
}
